rley SA (1995) Anastomotic leaks after low anterior resection for rectal carcinoma: evaluation with CT and barium enema. Am J Roentgenol 165:567&#x02013;571 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7645472</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hyman</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Manchester</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name><name><surname>Osler</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Burns</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Cataldo</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Anastomotic leaks after intestinal anastomosis: it&#x02019;s later than you think</article-title><source>Ann Surg</source><year>2007</year><volume>245</volume><fpage>254</fpage><lpage>258</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.sla.0000225083.27182.85</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Hyman N, Manchester TL, Osler T, Burns B, Cataldo PA (2007) Anastomotic leaks after intestinal anastomosis: it&#x02019;s later than you think. Ann Surg 245:254&#x02013;258 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17245179</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nicksa</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Dring</surname><given-names>RV</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>KH</given-names></name><name><surname>Sardella</surname><given-names>WV</given-names></name><name><surname>Vignati</surname><given-names>PV</given-names></name><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Anastomotic leaks: what is the best diagnostic imaging study?</article-title><source>Dis Colon Rectum</source><year>2007</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>197</fpage><lpage>203</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s10350-006-0708-x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Nicksa GA, Dring RV, Johnson KH, Sardella WV, Vignati PV, Cohen JL (2007) Anastomotic leaks: what is the best diagnostic imaging study? Dis Colon Rectum 50:197&#x02013;203 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17164970</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>Makin</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Reeve</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Ellenbogen</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Over-utilisation of radiography in the assessment of stapled colonic anastomoses</article-title><source>Eur J Radiol</source><year>1991</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>35</fpage><lpage>37</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0720-048X(91)90129-J</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Williams CE, Makin CA, Reeve RG, Ellenbogen SB (1991) Over-utilisation of radiography in the assessment of stapled colonic anastomoses. Eur J Radiol 12:35&#x02013;37 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1999207</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bruce</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Krukowski</surname><given-names>ZH</given-names></name><name><surname>Al-Khairy</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Russell</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>KG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Systematic review of the definition and measurement of anastomotic leak after gastrointestinal surgery</article-title><source>Br J Surg</source><year>2001</year><volume>88</volume><fpage>1157</fpage><lpage>1168</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.0007-1323.2001.01829.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Bruce J, Krukowski ZH, Al-Khairy G, Russell EM, Park KG (2001) Systematic review of the definition and measurement of anastomotic leak after gastrointestinal surgery. Br J Surg 88:1157&#x02013;1168 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11531861</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shorthouse</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bartram</surname><given-names>CI</given-names></name><name><surname>Eyers</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomson</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The water soluble contrast enema after rectal anastomosis</article-title><source>Br J Surg</source><year>1982</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>714</fpage><lpage>717</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/bjs.1800691210</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Shorthouse AJ, Bartram CI, Eyers AA, Thomson JP (1982) The water soluble contrast enema after rectal anastomosis. Br J Surg 69:714&#x02013;717 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7171972</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lucey</surname><given-names>BC</given-names></name><name><surname>Maher</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Boland</surname><given-names>GW</given-names></name><name><surname>Gervais</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Mueller</surname><given-names>PR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Percutaneous treatment by interventional radiologists of anastomotic leaks: basic concepts</article-title><source>Am J Roentgenol</source><year>2002</year><volume>179</volume><fpage>365</fpage><lpage>369</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Lucey BC, Maher MM, Boland GW, Gervais DA, Mueller PR (2002) Percutaneous treatment by interventional radiologists of anastomotic leaks: basic concepts. Am J Roentgenol 179:365&#x02013;369 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12130433</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>